{
  "utterance": "Jonas, retrieval-only is a step in the right direction, but \"contributor-approved\" needs detail. Who picks the excerpts: the library, or the contributor? I'd want contributors to choose or at least veto the passages and the surrounding context shown, not just tick a box on a list. A passage can read differently once the room around it is gone. Also: is anyone paid for this reuse? And withdrawal has to be quick and real, not \"next update.\" Theo, can the consent work include contributor time and a named person who handles objections? A facilitated listening event might suit some contributors better than a kiosk.",
  "cites": ["L2", "L3"],
  "memory": "Supports retrieval-only with contributor-chosen excerpts and context. Open: payment for contributors, fast withdrawal, named objection handler, and whether a facilitated listening event should be offered. Asked Theo about budgeting consent work."
}
